      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is a useful check: the split goes through `vma_set_split_offset()`, so it would catch /dev/zero taking the anonymous branch of `vma_slice_offset()`. As far as I can see, nothing else covers private /dev/zero offsets (`devzero_mthp_ppps.c` from aosp/4393905 only checks native mTHP).\n\nIt doesn\u0027t use `PR_SET_VMA_ANON_NAME`, though, so would you mind moving it into its own test, e.g. `devzero_slice_p3s.c`, rather than adding it to `anon_vma_name_ppps.c`?",
